treactor.netty-reactor-netty-http-1.3.0-e199857e\n\nThe initial metadata repair succeeded, but all three subsequent generation attempts failed because `generateMetadata -Pcoordinates=io.projectreactor.netty:reactor-netty-http:1.3.0` looked for the nonexistent `tests/src/io.projectreactor.netty/reactor-netty-http/1.3.0/build.gradle`; this version reuses the `1.0.39` test project. The attempted test edits were reverted, consistent with the metrics showing 3 iterations, 0 generated LOC, and identical starting/ending commits. Dynamic-access coverage is also unavailable because no `dynamic-access` output directory was produced. The original native failure is specifically `UnsupportedFeatureError: Support for Arena.ofShared is not active: enable with -H:+SharedArenaSupport`, rather than a conventional missing-metadata error.\n\nInspect:\n- `logs/io.projectreactor.netty:reactor-netty-http:1.3.0/issue-requested-metadata/pi-generation-2026-09-30T12-16-20-197072Z.log`\n- `logs/io.projectreactor.netty:reactor-netty-http:1.3.0/dynamic-access-report/generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport-2026-09-30T12-05-46-576160Z.log`\n- `logs/io.projectreactor.netty:reactor-netty-http:1.3.0/native-image-run-fix/fixTestNativeImageRun-2026-09-30T11-58-59-755612Z.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n- Correct or work around the test-version resolution so metadata generation targets the `1.0.39` test project while testing library version `1.3.0`.\n- Decide whether the WebSocket test should enable `-H:+SharedArenaSupport` or explicitly use heap-backed allocators, then run the full JVM/native test command.\n- Regenerate the dynamic-access report and verify the preserved `1.3.0` metadata before publication.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_07e02e8bc9e81352016abcfeee48a887d281377b2c3015b84f\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 18910, "output": 1017, "cacheRead": 132736, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 516,